    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1043">

                <pb facs="1407" n="1397" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg1397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 [Edwards, J. Dixon]: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Robertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-26T13:00:00+07:00">September 26,
                            1945—1 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 1:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1665. Edwards departed this morning for Hankow (Embassy’s 1628, September
                    20).</p>
                <p>Army has requested Consular officers be sent urgently to Canton and Hong Kong. We
                    replied no more men could be spared by Embassy but that officers sent by
                    Department to staff China Consulates are shortly expected arrive Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robertson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
